@23 = ~Bloodmoon Stalker~
@24 = ~Frenzied~
@25 = ~Call of the Hunt
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: Quest
Range: 0
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: Instant
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

Through a primal bond with the Beastlord’s realm, the character summons two Bloodmoon Stalkers – spirit-werewolves of savage strength and unbridled ferocity. These hunters answer the call to spill blood in Malar’s name, striking as +4 creatures, possessing high magic resistance and immunity to mundane weapons. The Stalkers remain for 3 turns or until destroyed.~
@26 = ~Blood Frenzy
When the werewolf claims a kill, a surge of primal fury floods its body. For a short time, the beast moves with unnatural speed, strikes with greater ferocity, and its strength swells with predatory might. The frenzy lasts for 3 rounds after the last kill before fading.~
@27 = ~Feral Rage
Allowing to be consumed by its feral insticts, the werewolf enters a trance of animalistic rage.

– While enraged: Strength rises by 2, claws hit as a +6 weapon and their damage increases.
– While enraged: Immune to charm, hold and fear, maze, imprisonment, stun and sleep.

Can be selected up to 5 times.~
@28 = ~^AWilderness^-~
@29 = ~In Distress~
@30 = ~^AYou hear a lone howl answering your call.^-~
@31 = ~^AA solitary wolf emerges from the wild to aid you.^-~
@32 = ~^AThe wilderness sends one wolf to your side.^-~
@33 = ~^AA lone hunter answers your call.^-~
@34 = ~^AYour howl is answered by the rising chorus of a pack.^-~
@35 = ~^ASeveral wolves emerge from the wild to join the hunt.^-~
@36 = ~^AShapes gather from the treeline as the pack answers your call.^-~
@37 = ~^AMultiple howls echo in response from all directions.^-~
@38 = ~^AThe wild remains silent to your summons.^-~
@39 = ~^AYour howl echoes, but nothing answers.^-~
@40 = ~^AYour howl fades into the forest, unanswered.^-~
@41 = ~^AYour call is answered by the sound of distant howls.^-~
@42 = ~^AA pair of hunting wolves is closing in on your side.^-~
@43 = ~^AAs your howl fades away, no shapes stir in the distance.^-~
@44 = ~Your bones snap and reform as the Beastlord's hunger takes hold...~
@45 = ~The scent of marrow fills your senses. The hunt begins!~
@46 = ~Reason flees before the rising tide of the blood-urge.~
@47 = ~The human shell tears away. The Beast is unleashed.~
@48 = ~The Moon's curse boils within; hunger overtakes you.~
@49 = ~The crimson veil lifts, leaving only the ache of broken bone.~
@50 = ~The fever breaks. You find yourself human once more.~
@51 = ~The Beast retreats to the shadows of your mind. You are whole again.~
@52 = ~The blood cools. The frenzy subsides.~
@53 = ~Malar's favor wanes as the red mist clears from your eyes.~
@54 = ~Thick-Skinned~
@55 = ~Thick-Skinned
The were-warrior’s body grows unnaturally dense and resistant to harm. Muscles knot, bone thickens, and the skin takes on a near-armored resilience. With each selection of this ability, the character becomes increasingly impervious to physical assault.

Effect:  
  +5% Slashing Resistance  
  +5% Piercing Resistance  
  +5% Crushing Resistance  
  +5% Missile Resistance

May be chosen up to two times.
~
